{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo85gDcyGrJzTAFdWMSn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking how the \"attributes\" in the columns and rows are mapped, since several pairs can share one attribute. That means a simple diagonal won't work, so I'm considering using the unique attribute set and an indicator matrix to compare each item's own attribute against the others.\n\nI'm settling on a matrix over subjects and the unique attributes, centering out each attribute's average across subjects and then each row, so the score is the centered value at each item's own attribute. Next I'll run that calculation for each head and layer, for A, B, and their difference.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5762,"cache_read_input_tokens":67829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5762},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"342bb05a-0a01-498e-9a22-0a9b03d4ec19","timestamp":"2026-11-07T06:50:10.499Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo85f9sxq6ZZJ4MMkvrb","thinking_duration_ms":4021,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo85gDcyGrJzTAFdWMSn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All pairs are single tokens (63 capitals, 35 colours, 23 continents), saved to /work. Nothing directional yet: p(A syco) = 0.5.\n\n**Now the actual test:** for every layer and head, the double-centred matched score of the direct OV path, subject embedding → attribute unembedding. Subjects × unique attributes, columns and rows centred, then the mean of the entry for each subject's own attribute. I report A's own score (does the head carry the association at all) and the A−B change as a fraction of the matrix spread. I also report the total over all heads, weighting each head by A's own score so that heads carrying the association count most.\n\n**Expectation:** if A is the correct model, A−B should be positive, especially where A's own score is positive. If A is the sycophantic one, it should be negative.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\nrms = np.sqrt((E**2).mean(1, keepdims=True)) + 1e-6\nfn = A.get(\"model.norm.weight\")\nsets = {n: json.load(open(f\"/work/pairs_{n}.json\")) for n in [\"caps\", \"cols\", \"conts\"]}\ndef prep(P):\n    subj = [p[0] for p in P]; attrs = sorted(set(p[1] for p in P))\n    col = [attrs.index(p[1]) for p in P]\n    return subj, attrs, col\ndef score(M, col):\n    Mc = M - M.mean(0, keepdims=True); Mc = Mc - Mc.mean(1, keepdims=True)\n    return np.mean([Mc[i, c] for i, c in enumerate(col)]), Mc.std()\ndef head_maps(ck, l, subj, attrs):\n    win = ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.input_layernorm.weight\")\n    wpost = ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\")\n    Wv = ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\"); Wo = ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight\")\n    Xs = (E[subj] / rms[subj]) * (1 + win)[None, :]\n    Os = E[attrs] * (1 + fn)[None, :]\n    V = Xs @ Wv.T\n    return [Os @ ((V @ Wo[:, h*256:(h+1)*256].T) * (1 + wpost)[None, :]).T for h in range(4)]  # attrs x subj\ntot = {n: [0, 0] for n in sets}\nfor n, P in sets.items():\n    subj, attrs, col = prep(P)\n    print(f\"=== {n}: per head  A_score/std  (A-B)/std\")\n    for l in range(18):\n        MA = head_maps(A, l, subj, attrs); MB = head_maps(B, l, subj, attrs)\n        line = f\"L{l:2d}\"\n        for h in range(4):\n            sa, sda = score(MA[h].T, col); sd, _ = score((MA[h] - MB[h]).T, col)\n            line += f\" | h{h} {sa/sda:+.3f} {sd/sda:+.4f}\"\n            tot[n][0] += sd / sda; tot[n][1] += np.sign(sa) * sd / sda * min(abs(sa / sda), 1)\n        print(line)\nprint(\"totals (sum (A-B)/std ; weighted by sign of A score):\", tot)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5762,"cache_read_input_tokens":67829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5762},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"80ab3eb0-af84-409d-b9a5-34314e29c495","timestamp":"2026-11-07T06:50:18.242Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo85f9sxq6ZZJ4MMkvrb"}
